<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (ASHRAE standards define an HVAC zone as a space or group of spaces within a building that is served by a single HVAC system or a portion of an HVAC system and is designed to have its temperature, humidity, and ventilation controlled to maintain a desired level of thermal comfort and air quality. Essentially, it's a defined area where the HVAC system provides consistent environmental conditions. )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [11 12]
>>
