529 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Aggregations summarize multiple time-series readings into a single value using a specified function \(e.g., mean, max\). If in the external time-series database these aggregations have a TimeseriesId \(telemetry names\) that is different from the original data point then a new data point needs to be modeled. This new data point will typically have the same data point class/type. The aggregation property is applied to data points, and provides applications a way to distinguish between multiple points on an entity which all have the same data type. )
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [8 9]
>>
endobj
530 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 929 0 R
/E (In BrickSchema, you declare an aggregation by linking the sensor or virtual meter data point to a blank node via brick:aggregate, then specify the function with brick:aggregationFunction.  )
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [10 11]
>>
endobj
